{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc","id":816135,"title":"Niktuku PC","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-25T08:35:16-08:00","id":816135,"title":"Niktuku PC","content":"Alright so would you allow a player to choose the Niktuku from the DAV20 book as a clan? Their weakness is they can drink from humans but they gain 1:3 ratio. But if they feed from a vampire they gain 1:1 for blood. Now this means they need to feed on vampires to keep active. This could be a big problem if your city does not have a lot of vampires and of course feeding on a vampire would cause issues with the fear of diablre and that is not even to bring up the idea of the Niktuku to the Nosferatu who are terrified of them and would likely try to kill them on sight.<br /> <br /> Sure with Bardo 3 they could feed on deer and cattle and gain some traction without leaving loads of humans bled dry laying around. Especially in a modern nights campaign a Nikituku with Bardo 3 could survive fairly easily with the right contacts. But other then that, how would it play out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10996-the-red-priest","name":"The Red Priest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T09:33:54-08:00","id":816176,"title":"","content":"I will never use it XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6052-rettile-blitch","name":"Rettile&Blitch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T09:44:52-08:00","id":816185,"title":"","content":"Personally I would be very hesitant in having a PC Niktuku, even the DAV20 version of them.<br /> <br /> As for the Bloodline weaknessesand Bardo, I wouldn't allow without a <i>very</i> good in-universe reason why this vampire of a rare bloodline has managed to learn the Discipline of another rare bloodline. And I'd probably make them pay for Bardo with XP or freebie points rather than having it as one of the PCs starting disciplines.<br /> <br /> But if I was to allow a PC Niktuku I wouldn't allow them to have Bardo. Having to deal with the Clan/Bloodline weakness is part of the game. How they deal with their dietary issues is an important matter that the player and PC should have figured out without resorting to such rare Disciplines that are unlikely to be found by most members of its Bloodline. If they haven't thought about that, than I would not allow the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T10:03:21-08:00","id":816203,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't see it as using a rare discipline to cover their weakness. Characters like rasalon and his site would have gladly befriended the children of Osiris. It would be prudent to try to learn it as much as a Nos learning obfuscate 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10996-the-red-priest","name":"The Red Priest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T10:40:17-08:00","id":816250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=816185#post816185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I would be very hesitant in having a PC Niktuku, even the DAV20 version of them.<br /> <br /> As for the Bloodline weaknesses and Bardo, I wouldn't allow without a <i>very</i> good in-universe reason why this vampire of a rare bloodline has managed to learn the Discipline of another rare bloodline. And I'd probably make them pay for Bardo with XP or freebie points rather than having it as one of the PCs starting disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do know that, though called a bloodline, they are actually more of a sect open to kindred of all origins as long as they shown the right mindset? Damn, there's even a canon setite archon NPC with it in the books! Also, it's quite dependent on Humanity, what would put extra complications and restrictions upon the character.<br /> <br /> But yes, i can understand how it might seem like pretty much of a cheap cop-out, specially if neither player nor ST has any serious intention of involving the Children in a chronicle. That said, we are speaking of Dark Ages - just grabbing 7th gen, some flaws and Animalism 6 [Animal Succulence] would be possible and <b>even more</b> of a cheap cop-out, giving basically the same benefits with no moral requirements or restrictions whatsoever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-25-2016, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T11:31:20-08:00","id":816290,"title":"","content":"I am not sure how actually PCable the Niktuku are. They are an antisocial bloodline given to treating kindred as kindred treat kine. As a group of pcs it could work, but in a more standard setup with other clans I can't imagine it working very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T11:49:20-08:00","id":816309,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's anything specifically <i>unplayable</i> about them... but using Bardo? The Children of Osiris are extremely rare, almost exclusive to Egypt and the Middle East.. which is far from the typically Niktuku realms. Bardo doesn't seem like a very reasonable option, honestly. I'd be <i>far</i> more hesitant about using Bardo in a campaign than using the Niktuku.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T11:55:58-08:00","id":816315,"title":"","content":"In Dark Ages where drinking vessels dry is the norm and many kindred dont walk the road od humanity it isn't too bad a weakness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T13:31:22-08:00","id":816391,"title":"","content":"Well see the idea of a niktuku as nothing more than monsters that hunt monsters the new take and the few Canon members have given them far more leeway. I am on my mobile or I would link the wiki profiles of the niktuku I am talking about. One is Rasalon and his sire Androvikus. Both seem to be reasonable and in fact are notes as having worked with other vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10996-the-red-priest","name":"The Red Priest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T14:55:08-08:00","id":816442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=816309#post816309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there's anything specifically <i>unplayable</i> about them... but using Bardo? The Children of Osiris are extremely rare, almost exclusive to Egypt and the Middle East.. which is far from the typically Niktuku realms. Bardo doesn't seem like a very reasonable option, honestly. I'd be <i>far</i> more hesitant about using Bardo in a campaign than using the Niktuku.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, their <b>roots </b>might be egyptian but i don't remember anything implying they are particularly more insular or landlocked than the Setites, quite the contrary on account of <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Milarepa\" target=\"_blank\">canon evidence</a>, in fact. Damn, the name they use for their discipline is a <b><i>tibetan </i></b>word, not egyptian, it's right the in Hunter's Hunted, for cryin' out loud.<br /> <br /> Their &quot;rarity&quot; is an artifact of the writers mostly ignoring their existence except for bits in Kemintiri's background than anything. They could be as small or large as the True Hand or Inconnu depending on a particular STs preferences. If the discipline cap = Humanity thing feels too lenient, double it or somesuch, requiring Humanity 6+ to keep <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Bardo\" target=\"_blank\">Gift of Apis</a> won't exactly be a cakewalk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-26-2026, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T19:19:46-08:00","id":816589,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of the reason they were downplayed is that they just didn't fit with the &quot;feel&quot; of Revised. They were introduced during the Superheroes-with-Fangs phase of VtM, along with the True Black Hand, Soul Eaters and a lot of other messy stuff. They mesh well with Mummy, but not so much with Vampire. The name of their Discipline being Tibetan is just another case of no-effort research, not an indication they actually spread to Tibet and learned Tibetan things and called their Discipline that for in-character reasons. <br /> <br /> Bardo, overall, just isn't a well-written or well-thought out Discipline. The Niktuku (DAV20) at least seem fairly solid, even if they are definitely more geared towards NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T20:42:51-08:00","id":816636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=816589#post816589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of the reason they were downplayed is that they just didn't fit with the &quot;feel&quot; of Revised. They were introduced during the Superheroes-with-Fangs phase of VtM, along with the True Black Hand, Soul Eaters and a lot of other messy stuff. They mesh well with Mummy, but not so much with Vampire. The name of their Discipline being Tibetan is just another case of no-effort research, not an indication they actually spread to Tibet and learned Tibetan things and called their Discipline that for in-character reasons.<br /> <br /> Bardo, overall, just isn't a well-written or well-thought out Discipline. The Nictuku (DAV20) at least seem fairly solid, even if they are definitely more geared towards NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, the tibetan connection is given in passing but clearly mentioned in Hunter's Hunted, as i pointed out previously, and reinforced by <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Milarepa\" target=\"_blank\">the one Children of Osiris NPC</a> in the books <b>being</b> a tibetan. Second, they came before Mummy and are more about ascetism and denial of the Beast &amp; its atrocities - something that was the exact opposite of Superhero-with-Fangs last time i checked - than millenia-long continuation/parody of egyptian mythology, unlike the mummies. They were downplayed long before Revised, as Khetamon, Milarepa - and maybe <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Samat_Ramal\" target=\"_blank\">a third</a> in Berlin by Night - with only one of these getting actual stats, being the only canon NPCs of the group shows. Even pre-KotE &quot;oriental vampires&quot; got two fully stated NPCs... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Considering the fact Bardo's point is one of eternal struggle/denial to contain the Beast instead of eventually finding balance/peace with it, one might even say they fit <b>better</b> with the &quot;feel&quot; of Revised than Golconda and the Inconnu. Conceptually at least - i do admit the discipline has issues (Restore Humanitas being the greatest, imho) - but that in itself is far from a shock considering it was printed for a book older than Clanbook: Brujah and has seen no revisions or updates ever since, afaik.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T23:21:36-08:00","id":816697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=816636#post816636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First, the tibetan connection is given in passing but clearly mentioned in Hunter's Hunted, as i pointed out previously, and reinforced by <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Milarepa&quot;]the</a> one Children of Osiris NPC[/URL] in the books <b>being</b> a tibetan. Second, they came before Mummy and are more about ascetism and denial of the Beast &amp; its atrocities - something that was the exact opposite of Superhero-with-Fangs last time i checked - than millenia-long continuation/parody of egyptian mythology, unlike the mummies. They were downplayed long before Revised, as Khetamon, Milarepa - and maybe <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Samat_Ramal&quot;]a</a> third[/URL] in Berlin by Night - with only one of these getting actual stats, being the only canon NPCs of the group shows. Even pre-KotE &quot;oriental vampires&quot; got two fully stated NPCs... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Considering the fact Bardo's point is one of eternal struggle/denial to contain the Beast instead of eventually finding balance/peace with it, one might even say they fit <b>better</b> with the &quot;feel&quot; of Revised than Golconda and the Inconnu. Conceptually at least - i do admit the discipline has issues (Restore Humanitas being the greatest, imho) - but that in itself is far from a shock considering it was printed for a book older than Clanbook: Brujah and has seen no revisions or updates ever since, afaik.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, their &quot;eternal struggle with the Beast&quot; allowed them to kill the BadGuysTM and then go back to high humanity by using a discipline... Restore Humanity is not an amendable flaw, but the core of their concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://silenceandwhispers.icyboards.net/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i65.tinypic.com/jpbv9t.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></span></span>","edited":{"userid":3552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3552-featherstone","user":"featherstone","date":". 01-26-2016, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3552-featherstone","name":"featherstone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T07:06:08-08:00","id":816848,"title":"","content":"I would keep them as a sect (cult/covenant really since they don't control cities) and just remove Bardo. Maybe recreate some of the powers of it as rituals or combo disciplines","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T07:12:08-08:00","id":816851,"title":"","content":"I wonder how Bardo 3 would work with the Noiad given they cannot drink from Animals and gain any blood of worth. Would this three dot make them completely weaknessless?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11059-father-darius","name":"Father Darius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T07:46:13-08:00","id":816870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>featherstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=816697#post816697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, their &quot;eternal struggle with the Beast&quot; allowed them to kill the BadGuysTM and then go back to high humanity by using a discipline... Restore Humanity is not an amendable flaw, but the core of their concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except then it isn't a real struggle - quick &quot;getaway from consequences&quot; card is my main problem with the discipline's <b>execution</b>, as the fluff doesn't imply &quot;easy patching up&quot; of Humanity as Restore Humanitas does, something made even worse by its being the level 1 power of the discipline. Reworked and/or at a higher level i might have less of a problem with it.<br /> <br /> But all of that said, i think the Children of Osiris main problem in the World of Darkness is probably being a sort of &quot;poor man Inconnu&quot;, what made them sort of redundant, what along with coming in a (quickly outstripped) hunter book served only to make them mostly obscure and were never really expanded and at the same time &quot;poor man Undying&quot;, as Horus and his people later took their mythic niche by assault and utterly dominated it by virtue of being something new and different.<br /> <br /> If i ever took the time to do something with them, i might simply things by making the Children into a faction of the Incconu, basically to use them as a springboard to expand - different ways and views of the struggle with the Beast, what function do the Monitors exactly serve for them as a whole, agendas &amp; interests of some cliques of ancients that can't quite let go of the world and Jyhad completely - and shine some light into the sect, what could be nice overall considering how terrible was Lair of the Hidden at doing so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Darius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=816851#post816851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how Bardo 3 would work with the Noiad given they cannot drink from Animals and gain any blood of worth. Would this three dot make them completely weaknessless?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, how does the Noiad weakness interact with Animal Succulence? I would guess this would be far more of an issue for DA games, considering 7th gen is relatively acessible from the get go, has no Humanity requirement and much less obscure - and consequently simpler to make an inattentive ST accept - than Bardo, not to mention that if you have Animal Succulence you're basically a master of Animalism too, what can be quite useful on itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T07:50:00-08:00","id":816876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Darius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=816851#post816851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how Bardo 3 would work with the Noiad given they cannot drink from Animals and gain any blood of worth. Would this three dot make them completely weaknessless?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the Ventrue, for that matter.<br /> <br /> I'd say it's up to the ST. Personally I'm not against characters who find a way to cope with their weakness, but on the other hand I'm suspicious of concepts that take a wildly exotic bloodline with a very crippling flaw, just to get rid of the flaw immediately. I mean, why do you want to play a Noiad who feeds from animals while you could play the same concept with a Gangrel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://silenceandwhispers.icyboards.net/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i65.tinypic.com/jpbv9t.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></span></span>","edited":{"userid":3552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3552-featherstone","user":"featherstone","date":". 01-26-2016, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3552-featherstone","name":"featherstone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T07:59:06-08:00","id":816885,"title":"","content":"Well I could see it play for my religious character. Perhaps they frenzied and killed someone they had grown to love, or a family member if they are a neonate. Such a trauma could make them want to search out these fabled vampires who could control their beast. Especially if rumors persisted of a discipline that would allow them to feed on animals instead and thus prevent another serious trauma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11059-father-darius","name":"Father Darius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T08:07:11-08:00","id":816891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Darius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=816885#post816885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I could see it play for my religious character. Perhaps they frenzied and killed someone they had grown to love, or a family member if they are a neonate. Such a trauma could make them want to search out these fabled vampires who could control their beast. Especially if rumors persisted of a discipline that would allow them to feed on animals instead and thus prevent another serious trauma.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see how that could work. However, do you need a Noiad to do that? Not saying it can't be done well, but a &quot;tragedy, guilt and redemption&quot; story could be done with literally any clan, while the Noiad have their own themes that in such a story have a high risk of being irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://silenceandwhispers.icyboards.net/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i65.tinypic.com/jpbv9t.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3552-featherstone","name":"featherstone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T08:14:51-08:00","id":816895,"title":"","content":"I am just saying if you wanted to play that character type you could. Perhaps you come from finnish stock and want to use related vampires to your native region. Or perhaps you like the idea of a vampire that was thought of as extinct being alive. The Sami where very important to the Noiad, they where their protectors during the midnight sun times. And they drew from the Sami for their childer so that storyline fits very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11059-father-darius","name":"Father Darius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T10:16:02-08:00","id":816970,"title":"","content":"I would never allow a Nicktuku PC, nor would I use them as presented in DAV20. I like them much better as the Nosferatu's boogeymen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10796-dismas","name":"Dismas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T19:41:09-08:00","id":817342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dismas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=816970#post816970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would never allow a Nicktuku PC, nor would I use them as presented in DAV20. I like them much better as the Nosferatu's boogeymen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your right to as it is the ST who defines what parts of the fluff that apply or not to the story it wants to tell. It's perfectly acceptable to veto certain character choices if they will bring elements one would find problematic - that said talking with the player to get a better idea of <b>why</b> that particular concept appealed to it can be helpful in finding common ground and steering the player towards alternatives more palatable or fitting to the chronicle.<br /> <br /> Or simply making a vanilla Nosferatu that strongly believes itself to be a secret tool - and maybe descendant - of one of the Nictuku, actual veracity of this conviction notwithstanding, with the PC being the tool of something else altogether (torpid elder/methuselah of any clan, old and powerful redcap, weird spirit of the Umbra, confusing and demented Wraith, Child of Night/Earthbound), the victim of a cruel Malkavian or clanmate prank gone wrong, pure and simple dementia, or a number of other alternatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-26-2016, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T07:39:11-08:00","id":817581,"title":"","content":"I have found that just about every concept will fit in to one of the 13 core DA clans, if not one of the basic 7 Camarilla clans. Bloodlines are simply an extra shiny bit on the character sheet that should come with a few terms and conditions before someone can play them. I'm not against them as a rule, but the Nicktuku are a special case - 4th Gen devoted servants of Abisimliard are not PC material. Someone playing a vanilla Nos that believed itself to be a descendant of a Nicktuku would be better, but they're still not going to be playing a Nicktuku.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10796-dismas","name":"Dismas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T08:03:45-08:00","id":817603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dismas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=817581#post817581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have found that just about every concept will fit in to one of the 13 core DA clans, if not one of the basic 7 Camarilla clans. Bloodlines are simply an extra shiny bit on the character sheet that should come with a few terms and conditions before someone can play them. I'm not against them as a rule, but the Nicktuku are a special case - 4th Gen devoted servants of Abisimliard are not PC material. Someone playing a vanilla Nos that believed itself to be a descendant of a Nicktuku would be better, but they're still not going to be playing a Nicktuku.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends if you rule they're all brainwashed mooks or if you assume they have personalities (as cases such as Rasalon would suggest). In the latter hypothesis they could be PC. Not the best PC material, and I'd ask why you want one anyway, but not entirely unplayable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://silenceandwhispers.icyboards.net/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i65.tinypic.com/jpbv9t.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3552-featherstone","name":"featherstone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T08:24:12-08:00","id":817624,"title":"","content":"Even if they have personalities, they are blood bound to their sire or otherwise controlled (Baba Yaga being the exception). I suppose in that case they could be PC material <i>if</i> the game were set in the second city or was a 4th gen game in general.<br /> <br /> Edit: Re: Rasalon/Androvikus - They aren't Nicktuku imo, just a couple of Nos that believe they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10796,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10796-dismas","user":"Dismas","date":". 01-27-2016, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10796-dismas","name":"Dismas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T08:41:22-08:00","id":817646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dismas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=817624#post817624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if they have personalities, they are blood bound to their sire or otherwise controlled (Baba Yaga being the exception). I suppose in that case they could be PC material <i>if</i> the game were set in the second city or was a 4th gen game in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totaly agree with you XD i love Nosferatu and the Nicktuku bloodline is a shit only to give more materials to the bored player XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6052-rettile-blitch","name":"Rettile&Blitch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:09:44-08:00","id":817722,"title":"","content":"Personally i have always prefered to take the Nictuku tale as more of myth with lots of imprecision and some kernels of fact than actual truth as a whole for a number of reasons in relation to the clan (puts them on worse footing than the Baali, makes their Founder too close to Shaitan &amp; Baal-the-Destroyer for confort, less to show for their efforts overall than the True Brujah) and the Niktuku as actual entities (so these people who were embraced millenia ago for being utterly ruthless, vicious bastards are still robotically loyal goons, though the Book of Nod tells us from the get-go that with enough time, enough will and enough hate, any bond can be broken - of what we have a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Sabbat\" target=\"_blank\">whole sect of psychos</a> as <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vaulderie\" target=\"_blank\">extra evidence</a> while utterly oblivious to the evident fact their sire prissy, petty cause, can only lead to their eventual consumption and doom?).<br /> <br /> So overall, not strongly attached to either take as the whole point is the Nictuku as boogeymen, feared and yet denied, sometimes believed but almost impossible to confirm or prove.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-07-2026, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:28:19-08:00","id":817740,"title":"","content":"As long as they aren't the DAV20 bloodline <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10796-dismas","name":"Dismas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:20:46-08:00","id":817825,"title":"","content":"It seems you can trace Rasalon and his sire back to their Ante. So why would they say they where Niktuku and not be?<br /> I mean the legends of the Niktuku say they are all strictly blood bonded to their masters... if their master does not have the genecidal ideals then why would they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10996-the-red-priest","name":"The Red Priest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:38:16-08:00","id":817839,"title":"","content":"Androvikus could have been lying, misled, or Dominated in to believing he was the childe of a Nicktuku. That information is from a fluff piece iirc, so it is not necessarily true. Or maybe he was, and Nicktuku is simply a term defined as &quot;Abisimiliard's blood-bound 4th gen childer who are in every way just Nosferatu, albeit mighty powerful ones&quot;. Would be useful to have a Manchurian Lineage within the Nos Clan at large if genocide was the goal. Still no need for a bloodline. Androvikus and Rasalon could have been unsuspecting dupes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10796-dismas","name":"Dismas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:47:40-08:00","id":817850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dismas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=817740#post817740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as they aren't the DAV20 bloodline <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>As i don't have DAV20 yet, can't really opine on that aspect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dismas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=817839#post817839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Androvikus could have been lying, misled, or Dominated in to believing he was the childe of a Nicktuku. That information is from a fluff piece iirc, so it is not necessarily true. Or maybe he was, and Nicktuku is simply a term defined as &quot;Abisimiliard's blood-bound 4th gen childer who are in every way just Nosferatu, albeit mighty powerful ones&quot;. Would be useful to have a Manchurian Lineage within the Nos Clan at large if genocide was the goal. Still no need for a bloodline. Androvikus and Rasalon could have been unsuspecting dupes.</div> </div> </div> </div>To quote a wise lady's <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OawrlVoQqSs\" target=\"_blank\">words</a>... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My feeling on the matter might or not change after i look at them in the book. As an aside, i think the Nicktuku as boogeymen lineage within the clan itself is already referenced in the Libellus Sanguini series, though i would have to check out for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-27-2016, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:50:00-08:00","id":817921,"title":"","content":"The DAV20 bloodline is distinct from the core clan, with different Disciplines and a different Flaw. It plays very loose with established lore (like much of the book).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10796-dismas","name":"Dismas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T14:11:30-08:00","id":817947,"title":"","content":"I like the possibility implied in <i>New York by Night</i>: the Niktuka are a case of the Nosferatu mistaking various monstrous opportunistic predators (like the Tzimisce antediluvian's shoggoth-esque form under Manhattan) as servants of their own founder pursuing a vendetta against them, when in fact they're just getting targeted because they favor underground locations out of the sight of humanity (also favored by said monstrously inhuman predators).<br /> <br /> It opens the door for a runaway vozhd, a coagulated gestalt of Blood Brothers, or something similar also being mistaken for their legendary enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","user":"Matt the Bruins fan","date":". 01-27-2016, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:09:35-08:00","id":818027,"title":"","content":"What is funny is a Niktuku can have a Appearance score higher then 0. They lose a dot of that to a physical stat every Century but really they could be passibly normal.. you think they would be overrunning the world. Same for the Noiad and their near lack of a weakness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10996-the-red-priest","name":"The Red Priest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T05:55:23-08:00","id":818363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=817947#post817947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the possibility implied in <i>New York by Night</i>: the Niktuka are a case of the Nosferatu mistaking various monstrous opportunistic predators (like the Tzimisce antediluvian's shoggoth-esque form under Manhattan) as servants of their own founder pursuing a vendetta against them, when in fact they're just getting targeted because they favor underground locations out of the sight of humanity (also favored by said monstrously inhuman predators).<br /> <br /> It opens the door for a runaway vozhd, a coagulated gestalt of Blood Brothers, or something similar also being mistaken for their legendary enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, truth be told, i have always toyed with that kind of option myself - how no matter how well-informed not even Nosferatu know it all, so a lot of things that move and prey on unknown underground dwellers might be mistaken for the Nictuku or associated with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-28-2016, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T06:42:15-08:00","id":818386,"title":"","content":"why not both? because it's only merchandise strategy to sell much more copy of is DAV20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6052-rettile-blitch","user":"Rettile&amp;Blitch","date":". 01-28-2016, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6052-rettile-blitch","name":"Rettile&Blitch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T07:20:26-08:00","id":818403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=817947#post817947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the possibility implied in <i>New York by Night</i>: the Niktuka are a case of the Nosferatu mistaking various monstrous opportunistic predators (like the Tzimisce antediluvian's shoggoth-esque form under Manhattan) as servants of their own founder pursuing a vendetta against them, when in fact they're just getting targeted because they favor underground locations out of the sight of humanity (also favored by said monstrously inhuman predators).<br /> <br /> It opens the door for a runaway vozhd, a coagulated gestalt of Blood Brothers, or something similar also being mistaken for their legendary enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly a possibility, and a good approach to take for some interesting stories, but I'd see it as 1.) the Nicktuku are the loyal childer of the Nos Ante out to destroy the disloyal childer and their spawn and 2.) the Nos mistake other things for being Nicktuku every now and then, instead of 1.) The Nosferatu myths of the Nicktuku are merely a collection of tales about them bumping in to the horrors that lie deep in the earth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=817850#post817850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As i don't have DAV20 yet, can't really opine on that aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would recommend only buying the PDF, and then only if it is on sale. I regret backing the KS for a deluxe copy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10796-dismas","name":"Dismas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T08:07:09-08:00","id":818431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Red Priest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=818027#post818027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is funny is a Niktuku can have a Appearance score higher then 0. They lose a dot of that to a physical stat every Century but really they could be passibly normal.. you think they would be overrunning the world. Same for the Noiad and their near lack of a weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the thing is, that isn't their primary weakness, just a secondary one. In fact its one that you wouldn't see come into play unless you're playing a game that spans centuries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=818363#post818363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, truth be told, i have always toyed with that kind of option myself - how no matter how well-informed not even Nosferatu know it all, so a lot of things that move and prey on unknown underground dwellers might be mistaken for the Nictuku or associated with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I have similar thoughts. Back in the Rev Ed era when I first read about the Nictuku, I liked and disliked them. On the one hand, I liked the idea of this Nosferatu boogeyman, whether real or imagined, haunting them. But I don't like that they are ancient 4th Gen vampires that no coterie could stand any hope of standing against. In fact I vaguely remember one adventure in I think <i>Nights of Prophecy</i> that involves the coterie witnesses Baba Yaga's at the hands of one of the Nictuku and if there's a Nos in the party, they're basically dead shortly there after because the Nictuku will kill them next.<br /> <br /> To me, the DAV20 Nictuku are the ideal form of the Nictuku to use in chronicles. They aren't unstatable monsters of insane and impossible power but contain a lot of the same menace as vampires that target other vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T08:34:48-08:00","id":818455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=817850#post817850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My feeling on the matter might or not change after i look at them in the book. As an aside, i think the Nicktuku as boogeymen lineage within the clan itself is already referenced in the Libellus Sanguini series, though i would have to check out for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=818431#post818431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To me, the DAV20 Nictuku are the ideal form of the Nictuku to use in chronicles. They aren't unstatable monsters of insane and impossible power but contain a lot of the same menace as vampires that target other vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>[QUOTE=AkatsukiLeader13;n818431]<br /> <br /> Libellus Sanguinis VI offers two possibilities. That they are agents of the methuselahs that use that cover for betterment of the clan. And that there might be an unseen faction hunting the Nos <br /> Actually there is a third if you count the tale of Fair Ymir. It worth looking into just to use Mother's Milk running sour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T02:37:19-08:00","id":819069,"title":"","content":"My personal solution is the next one: I think there are two warring broods of the Antediluvian: the Nictuku (Gorgo, Nuckalavee and others), allied with him, and the Nosferatu, the descendents of three Mathusalens (Baba Yaga, the Matriarch and the Maiden in the River) that fight againts him . The Nosferatu, allied with the Camarilla and the mayority in Europe and Near East, fight against the Nictuku and their &quot;loyalists&quot; broods, the Nosferatu of America, the Far East and subsaharian Africa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T07:42:29-08:00","id":819237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=818431#post818431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, the DAV20 Nictuku are the ideal form of the Nictuku to use in chronicles. They aren't unstatable monsters of insane and impossible power but contain a lot of the same menace as vampires that target other vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue the opposite. Lacking definition, they are much more menacing than something that has been reduced to a playable splat. If you want the menace of vampires that target other vampires you could use Assamites.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10796-dismas","name":"Dismas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T16:24:12-08:00","id":1554991,"title":"","content":"Doing some thread necromancy here. I got permission from my master to play a Niktuku in rhe next chronicle. I don't know a lot about the bloodline beyond what is in the VDA20 manual and on the white wold fandom page. I was looking for a clan with simple, common disciplines, and Auspex, Potence and Celerity was my favourite combo.<br /> <br /> The gradual loss of Appearance dots means gradual free increase of physical dots. Needing 3 times the amount of human blood is easy to solve, and easier if you take the Herd background, which fits their habits according to VDA20. You're trained to hunt, so human preys should not be an issue anyway.<br /> <br /> I'm more concerned about whether I need an alternative identify among Cainites, pretending to belong to another clan...thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T18:17:23-08:00","id":1554996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=1554991#post1554991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more concerned about whether I need an alternative identify among Cainites, pretending to belong to another clan...thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>You will absolutely need to pretend to be part of another clan. The Nosferatu hate and fear the Niktuku and will no doubt try and capture/kill your character at the first opportunity, Prince and Laws be damned. I would give the PC the flaw Clan Enmity (Nosferatu) and Dark Secret (Real Identity).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T23:37:44-08:00","id":1555002,"title":"","content":"There is a funny &quot;anomaly&quot;<br /> Libellus Sanguinis 4: Thieves in the Night, gives us <b>Melachoate</b><br /> Now he is a 4th Generation Nosferatu, Child of Absimiliard and since he is not Yima, Baba Yaga (tho she indeed considered a Nictuku) or the Matriarch... he is firmly in the &quot;Yeah, he is a Nictuku&quot; category<br /> But like Baba Yaga had Gutka, the Salt Queen, Melitta Wallenberg, Poison Tooth, the Black Spiral Dancer Abomination (yikes) and Sergei Voshkov to name a few (not to mention IF Baba Yaga IS the Matriarch; tho' they are probably not the same and the Matriarch indeed the main progenitor of the Clan, since his first Child, Angiwar is <i>older</i> than Baba Yaga by a millenium or so) <b>Melachoate </b>also have a progeny <b>Androvikus </b>who told his childe, <b>Rasalon</b> that not all of the Nictuku were evil monsters of legend, and that this depiction of the bloodline was used by the eldest among the Nosferatu to frighten the young and ensure their obedience...<br /> <br /> Nor <b>Androvikus </b>nor <b>Rasalon</b> hid or denied their lineage, but claiming and admitting you are a Nictuku is probably as wise as claiming and admitting you are Baali, BUT it is only something that the Nosferatu care about; all the other Clan?<br /> Would just shrug, good for you, now made your oath and let me see what you are good for<br /> <br /> So we have at least two Nictuku, Baba Yaga and Melachoate who are self-admitted Nictuku, one of them escaped the Blood Bond, the other? Eh, not that much, both sired and never hid the fact who is their Sire and their kids technically a Nictuku &quot;bloodline&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you are a 4th Generation Nictuku? You have options.<br /> Be like Vasilisa, your Sire's enforcer and assassin, hunter of the Clan or... like Baba Yaga or Melachoate, Nictuku who is not that much of a monster from the dawn of time Embraced by a vain prick<br /> Clan Enmity (Nosferatu) is basically a must anyway<br /> Working out your background also important; what ancient monster of a bygone era you were that attracted the attention of Absilimiard to Embrace you as his elite task force of Monsters first to kill Zillah, then when it not really worked to hunt down the Clan in a futile hope killing all of the ugly bastards will pelase Caine to lift his course... including but not limited to you of course at the end.<br /> (If you want to give a twist, the Guruhi-Nosferatu connection is a treasuretove of legends and possible explanations/misinterpretations. The Guruhi are mostly unified, despite an old legend which says there are two &quot;lines&quot; of Guruhi. The second line was supposed to take over Africa, replacing the original line when it was deemed &quot;unfit&quot;. These two lines of Guruhi could be the Guruhi and the Nictuku, and from the other line, the Nictuku branched out the Nosferatu, but still in the Guruhi's eyes could be seen as the lignering threat that will take over and always watch... always...)<br /> If you are farther down the line it is not that hard, you are just a strong Nosferatu<br /> <br /> The Vampire: The Dark Ages 20th Anniversary Edition Niktuku not necesarily the same as the Nictuku (with a C) and they are probably - or at least heinted to be - a Bloodline from Baba Yaga with who only sate their thirst with the blood of one kind of victim: other Cainites.<br /> <br /> So your flaws, merits, background and potential Dark Fate is really tied to who you really are?<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 11-03-2025, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T01:58:16-08:00","id":1555014,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a><br /> The character is 7th gen from the DAV20 playable Niktuku. They are presented as progeny of Baba Yaga, hunt down Nosferatus preferably but also other vampires and are often bound to their sire or ancestors or Absimiliard (I can't remember how it was phrased exactly).<br /> <br /> My idea for a playable one in a coterie was to have his sire pose as a Toreador for centuries, so he officially comes off as Toreador. Both clans have Auspex and Celerity and both value beauty in Infants. The lack of talent in Presence can be explained as a quirky lack of social engagement compared to most Toreador, with hunting and fighting being treated as a form of art. One dot in Alternative Identity would be all that is required to be accepted as a quirky Toreador in the Domain as long as I and my Sire don't draw attention to ourselves.<br /> <br /> I don't think Clan Enmity (Nosferatu) would be a must: obviously if you let slip that you are Niktuku and want Nosferatu vitae, some will come for you if you look weak, but the basis of their relationship as I understand it is that 1) the Niktuku avoid drawing attention, either isolating themselves from Cainites or pretending to be from another clan; 2) Nosferatus don't hunt for Niktuku, they simply try to survive them and play defensively. Other clans don't know or don't care, unless they discover a serial killer of Cainites, in which case the punishment is the same regardless of clan or bloodline.<br /> <br /> As hunters, their discipline spread is quite effective. Sure, they miss out on Obfuscate, but they can still hide with a massive pool of Dexterity + Stealth + Celerity and having extra blood per turn to pump Dexterity. A surprise attack with both Potence and Celerity is potentially fatal and can be struck at a distance (thrown weapons). Auspex obviously helps hunting prey anywhere, each power in its own way. Young ones are not hideous and can hide comfortably in plain sight.<br /> <br /> Generally, allowing for 7th and higher gen Niktuku means putting them on the same level as normal characters, because the Niktuku's main advantage to be boogeymen is their age and low gen. Between an Assamite and Niktuku of similar age and gen, the Assamite is probably more dangerous. Even a Warrior of Glycon is more dangerous.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T03:17:05-08:00","id":1555016,"title":"","content":"Yeah, their unique Discipline spread and lack of traditional Nosferatu weakness is why I throw in the possible Guruhi connection <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you want to pose as a Toreador, like your Sire then .. .well...<br /> <i>Clan Impersonation</i> is a very tricky thing to do<br /> <br /> There is actually a secondary ability for it and while Alternative Identity beckground is not bad (tho' I would say 1 is not enough, but it is just me) there are other options<br /> <br /> Clan Impersonation (it is from Clan Book Assamite - but I think it is safe to say any vampire who wants to impersonate probably knows this)<br /> This is the ability to imitate the characteristics of another clan sufficiently well to be mistaken for a member. It involves changes to behavior, knowledge of clan jargon and politics, and sometimes and element of physical disguise as well.<br /> \u2022 Novice: Fool anyone who hasn't had direct dealings with the clan<br /> \u2022\u2022 Practiced: Fool anyone who is slightly familiar with the clan<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Competent: Fool a clan neonate<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Expert: Fool a clan ancillae<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Master: Fool a clan elder<br /> <br /> Still, while the Nosferatu not actively hunt the Nictuku they are - depending of the local warren - would keep track of any suspicious activites and signs of a potential Nictuku<br /> Dark Secret as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\">AnubisXy</a> said is kind of a given, and if it comes out would trigger the Clan Enmity (Nosferatu)<br /> To be fair, as a Toreador pretender you should have the Clan Enmity (Nosferatu) regardless of your liniage, because it actually would reinforce your Alternative Identity as a Toreador (see? those plaguerats hate me for my eerie beauty, oh woe me...)<br /> And in the Dark Ages it was not that easy to get a large quantity of blood you need to function, even with a Herd (keep in mind the Herd tend to stay in one place and the longer you are a place it is ether more difficult or either more easy to impersonate a clan, depending on your ST)<br /> Sooner or later you will attract attention, people vanish, your have to eat a Cainite or two... maybe even diableire... so you are up for a ride\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 11-03-2025, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T21:39:16-08:00","id":1555047,"title":"","content":"No. Makes little sense.<br /> <br /> And how are they gonna learn Bardo? Probably 10 vampires in the whole world who know it and what makes the PC special enough to be a Chosen One? Pass.<br /> <br /> And plus at my Tables, Niktuku arent real vamps but rather a Discipline combo power ole Nosferatu/Absimilliard uses to keep his kids sharp and on edge.<br /> Good ole Abs was a supreme hunter and knows how fragile apex predators are, the value of networks and teamwork, and keeps his kids focused on survival instead of dalliances' like most other clans. Interesting how the Animalism Clans arent too preoccupied with fashion, style, and beautiful food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T20:33:32-08:00","id":1557535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Red Priest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc#post816135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright so would you allow a player to choose the Niktuku from the DAV20 book as a clan?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No. The Niktuku are the childer of Absimiliard, which means they are all 4th generation, and are EXTREMELY ANCIENT. I believe the child who killed Baba Yaga is supposed to be around 14,000 years or so?<br /> <br /> Also, they exist for the singular goal of exterminating the Nosferatu. Which means they aren't going to be playing nice with any of the three main sects, if they have a Nosferatu population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T04:48:47-08:00","id":1557542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=1557535#post1557535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No. The Niktuku are the childer of Absimiliard,</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nictuku, yes<br /> <br /> But what he was talking about were the &quot;Niktuku&quot; with a &quot;K&quot;<br /> Vampire: The Dark Ages 20th Anniversary Edition presented this Bloodline<br /> According to the V20 version, the Niktuku are somehow related to the witch Baba Yaga - they are called &quot;witches of Baba Yaga,&quot;- , and can only sate their thirst with the blood of one kind of victim: other Cainites. Their origins remain questionable at best, according to the book itself.<br /> With their own strange apperance and weakness<br /> <br /> For reasons best known to the bloodline alone, they tend to select the most beautiful youths they can find, grabbing up particularly fetching youths and maids from any village close to the havens. They prefer these youths just at the cusp of adulthood, the blurry line between child and adult. The Hungry possess a great eeriness, though few see them long enough to put a finger on why. They are wide-eyed, their skin too perfect, their teeth too white, their fingers too long and graceful. Both their hunger and their beauty are inhuman.<br /> The Hungry - as the Bloodline is called - suffer from an inability to gain sustenance from kine blood. For every three blood points they drain, they gain only one to their system. Cainite vitae nourishes them normally. Additionally, age is difficult and transforming on the bloodline. For every hundred years since their Embrace, the Hungry lose a point from their Appearance Attribute. That dot does not vanish; instead, it moves to any one Physical Attribute that can bear the increase. They grow slowly but decidedly bent, twisted, and deadly, slowly aging grotesques that blame the Nosferatu for their condition.<br /> It is not a flaw persee but the Hungry will not haven where they cannot see the moon when they rise and leave each night.<br /> <br /> It is a bit blurry where the Nictuku ends and the Niktuku starts since the Nictuku were believed to be composed exclusively of vampires of the fourth generation but that was disputed by the biography of Rasalon and his sire Androvikus, that appeared in the book Libellus Sanguinis 4: Thieves in the Night<br /> Also Mnemach, a 6th Generation Nosferatu - part of the <i>Parisii</i> breed, which left her skin translucent and all veins, nerves and muscles visible to the naked eye - from France by Night and Libellus Sanguinis 4: Thieves in the Night also called herself a Nictuku<br /> (In her case it is possible she was the descendant of <b>Nuckalavee, </b>the Skinless One (the most gruesome about his appearance is the fact that he has no skin. Black blood courses through yellow veins and the pale sinews and powerful muscles are clear to see. He has an aversion of running water and those who are chased by him have only to cross a stream to get rid of him.) and it is possible he is the ancestor to the Parisii breed of the Nosferatu)<br /> <br /> But in this case he topic was about the DAV20 Bloodline<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T06:19:58-08:00","id":1557545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/816135-niktuku-pc?p=1557542#post1557542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Nictuku, yes<br /> <br /> But what he was talking about were the &quot;Niktuku&quot; with a &quot;K&quot;<br /> Vampire: The Dark Ages 20th Anniversary Edition presented this Bloodline<br /> According to the V20 version, the Niktuku are somehow related to the witch Baba Yaga - they are called &quot;witches of Baba Yaga,&quot;- , and can only sate their thirst with the blood of one kind of victim: other Cainites. Their origins remain questionable at best, according to the book itself.<br /> With their own strange apperance and weakness<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, she really, really loves pissing off her sire, doesn't she?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T09:19:54-08:00","id":1557547,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this is random and if it has already been said. I just happened to glance at this thread and something came to mind: the fact that the Niktuku can only drink Cainite blood seems linked to the idea that Absimiliard was specifically responsible for the diablerie of the 2nd gen, which I remember being a thing somewhere in the lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T09:33:12-08:00","id":1557548,"title":"","content":"Yes<br /> Absimilliard, a goodlooking hunter hunt for sabrethoots (the Sabrethoot died out before 11000 BC), Zillah hunt down Absimilliard, and Embraced him. For the tiny little scar, Absimilliard hates his Sire with passion [Cb-N p.13]<br /> Absimilliard (after sneaked up on Tzimisce who had discovered how to conrol his progeny through bloodbond) give the Embrace to several creatures, and creates the Nictuku. Only one girl can escape before the bond, she, the Matriarch become the progenitor of the Clan Nosferatu [Cb-N p.14]<br /> \u200bAbsimilliard invents the theory of Diablerie from Hunter belifes. He had been a hunter, and he firmly belived that when he caught and ate something, he gained its spirit and power. So if he could get a hold of a vampire.... He fooled Caine with Obfuscate. Caine belived his story about a wolf-men attack, and become angry, swearing vengeance on the wolf-creature, he leaving the City to its own. [Cb-N p.15]<br /> \u200b Absimilliard attacked Zillah while Caine is away with the Nictuku and tried to Diableriesed his sire. Caine retruns in time and beat the crap out his grandchildren. He curses Absimilliard with ugliness (Nosferatu weakness) and banish him from the First City [Cb-N p.15-16 / CbR-N . p.18-19] (Zillah survived this)<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}